Subject: [PATCH 04776/11362] [outer-loop] ARC leaderboard comparison: top
 "leaders" use NO frontier model (premise inverted)

Operator asked how the cloned top-leaderboard projects succeed with frontier models while Carnot fails.
9-agent comparative read of every cloned solver (adversarial-verified, premise SUPPORTED): the premise is
inverted. The top numbers (nihilisticneuralnet 0.46, vyankteshdwivedi 0.39) use ZERO LLM and win by a
white-box exploit (importlib.exec_module the game's own source + set_level teleport + read ground-truth
win flags) on the PUBLIC set; StochasticGoose (winner 12.58%) + just-explore (3rd) use no LLM either.
Where frontier IS the core solver (official templates, OpenClaw) there is zero banked score; frontier-LLM
agents score <0.4% hidden (arXiv:2603.24621). Scores are not apples-to-apples: Carnot 0.08 = RHAE hidden
set via blind live discovery; valid hidden comparators (StochasticGoose 0.25%, frontier <0.4%) put Carnot
comparable-to-AHEAD of the legitimate field. Carnot and frontier-LLM hit the SAME hidden-win-state wall;
leaders only look better via an easier set + a source-reading mechanism Carnot is forbidden to use.
Borrowable (legit): just-explore graph-routing + salience priors; NOT the source-read cheat.

